## Notes / Cross-Checks & Discrepancies Flagged

<div style="border-left:4px solid #1E3A8A;background:#EFF6FF;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>GWP basis caveat:</b> H1FY25 (6 months to Sep-30-2024) predates the IRDAI-mandated 1/n long-term premium accounting change, which the company's own disclosures confirm took effect "w.e.f. October 1, 2024." Hence the <b>₹3,241.5 cr</b> GWP figure is the single applicable statutory basis for this period — there is no dual ex-1/n vs. 1/n reporting for H1FY25, so it is reported as-is rather than left blank.
</div>

- **Claims ratio rounding:** Statutory filing reports <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">62.46%</span> (YTD Sep-30-2024) vs. the investor deck's rounded 62.5% — the statutory figure is used per source-authority hierarchy.
- **Combined ratio rounding:** Statutory <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">103.47%</span> vs. deck's rounded 103.5% — statutory figure used.
- **Net worth:** Statutory balance-sheet components (Paid-up equity ₹1,71,768 lakh + Reserves & Surplus ₹34,687 lakh + Share Application Money ₹4 lakh + Fair Value Change A/c ₹(0) lakh) sum to **₹2,06,459 lakh = ₹2,064.59 cr**, consistent with the deck's rounded ₹2,064.6 cr KPI figure — no material discrepancy.
- **Commission ratio and IFRS-basis claims ratio** are genuinely not disclosed as named metrics in either the statutory Reg 33/52 statement or the H1FY25 investor deck (only "Net Commission" absolute ₹ value and "Combined Ratio/Claims Ratio" IGAAP-basis percentages are shown) — left blank per instructions rather than estimated/derived.
- **Compliance filings (CO/RTA/Grievance Report):** Contain no GWP/PAT/ratio data — Compliance Officer: Mr. Rajat Sharma, Company Secretary; RTA: KFin Technologies Limited; Investor complaints for the quarter: **0** received, **0** pending, **0** disposed, **0** unresolved.
- **IRDAI NL-1/NL-2 standalone disclosure PDF for Sep-2024** could not be independently located as a separate document on the current IR site structure; the statutory Reg 33/52 financial results statement (filed per IRDAI circular IRDAI/F&A/CIR/LFTD/027/01/2017, which carries the same statutory ratios NL disclosures would show) was used instead as the authoritative statutory source for NWP, NEP, EoM ratio, Net worth and Solvency ratio.

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Key takeaway:</b> H1FY25 shows a <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">mixed</span> underwriting picture — statutory IGAAP PAT was <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">marginally negative (-₹5.8 cr)</span> against a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">positive IFRS-basis PAT of ₹59.5 cr</span>, reflecting valuation/consolidation differences between the two bases. The <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">combined ratio of ~103.5%</span> indicates underwriting losses were still being absorbed by investment income, while solvency at <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">2.25x</span> remained comfortably above the regulatory minimum.
